# SKILL.md files allowed to contain `${`, each with its reason.
#
# Gemini CLI rewrites every `${name}` in an extension's skill text before the model reads it,
# using its own variables (extensionPath, workspacePath, /, pathSeparator), the values of the
# settings declared in gemini-extension.json, and every key of a trusted workspace's .env file.
# That last set is unbounded, so scripts/lint-skills.py rejects `${` in every SKILL.md that is
# not listed here. A listed file still may not use Gemini's own names or a declared setting.
# An entry whose file no longer contains `${` is reported as a note, not an error, so a skill
# can drop the syntax in its own PR without breaking the integration branch.
skills/domino-launchers/SKILL.md        # Domino Launcher command syntax: one ${name} placeholder per form field
